# Channel Dumps Directory

Place raw channel data exports here.

## Expected Format

Each channel should have a JSON file with this structure:

```json
{
  "channel": "@ChannelHandle",
  "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@ChannelHandle",
  "subscriber_count": 500000,
  "total_videos": 150,
  "extracted_date": "2026-01-10",
  "videos": [
    {
      "video_id": "dQw4w9WgXcQ",
      "title": "Video Title Here",
      "views": 1000000,
      "likes": 50000,
      "comments": 5000,
      "publish_date": "2025-06-15",
      "duration_seconds": 720,
      "thumbnail_url": "https://...",
      "description": "First 200 chars of description..."
    }
  ]
}
```

## How to Get This Data

### Option 1: YouTube Data API v3 (Recommended)
1. Create a Google Cloud project
2. Enable YouTube Data API v3
3. Create API credentials
4. Use the channels.list and search.list endpoints

### Option 2: Third-Party Tools
- vidIQ: Export channel analytics
- TubeBuddy: Export competitor data
- Social Blade: Historical data

### Option 3: Manual Collection
For small datasets, manually record:
- Video titles
- View counts
- Publish dates
- Durations

## File Naming Convention

`{channel_handle}_{date}.json`

Example: `@HistoryChannel_2026-01-10.json`
